337	// detection included) has passed. A pass rejected on a node examined later,
338	// or by the cycle check that runs last — even for an edge on an untaken
339	// branch or an entry-unreachable node — never replaces any entry: the
340	// relations of the most recent SUCCESSFUL validation survive, so a parked
341	// run cannot be rerouted by an edit the caller never got accepted, and a
342	// later restore of the definition needs no second validation. Keyed by node
